## Context

`data/capability_timeline.csv` currently records Alibaba stage 3
(Browsing / web search) as `absent`, the decision frozen by ticket 0232
/ PR #426 after the 2025-03-07 Qwen-Agent QwQ-32B demo was rejected as
a developer SDK, not a consumer product.

A dead-agent salvage (t0229-research-absent-cells, killed mid-commit
2026-05-22) surfaced a *different* primary source that 0232 never
evaluated: the Qwen Chat v0.2 launch on chat.qwen.ai, announced via
the `@Alibaba_Qwen` X handle on 2025-01-24 with built-in web search.
That post is `x.com/Alibaba_Qwen/status/1882818582758961351`. The
snowflake-decoded timestamp is 2025-01-24T15:51 UTC. The launch is
cross-confirmed by the 2025-01-27 `qwen2.5-1m` blog which references
Qwen Chat as supporting "perform searches".

This is a consumer-product launch on Alibaba's official channel — it
meets the stage-3 methodology threshold (launch in a public commercial
product, primary source from the lab itself). The X post is the
primary source; the format is the same one the matrix already accepts
for Alibaba stage 5 (Deep Research on Qwen Chat, also sourced from
`@Alibaba_Qwen` X — see bibliography entry [31]).

## Actions

1. Update Alibaba stage-3 row in `data/capability_timeline.csv` from
   `absent` to `2025-01-24, primary-blog, qwen-chat-v02-2025`.
2. Add bibliography entry [42] in `docs/capability-timeline.md`
   pointing to `x.com/Alibaba_Qwen/status/1882818582758961351`.
3. Update the prose matrix cell (Alibaba × stage 3) in
   `docs/capability-timeline.md` from `absent` to the new dated entry.
4. Remove the stage-3 absence line from the Alibaba bullet in the
   "Honest gaps and divergences" section (lines ~206-232).
5. Regenerate `slides/inputs/generated/fig_capability_timeline.pdf`
   via `uv run python -m aedist.plot_capability_timeline`.
6. Verify `tests/test_capability_timeline.py` and
   `tests/test_capability_timeline_sync.py` pass.

## Findings (quoted from t0229 research notes, dead-agent worktree
agent-a7857d2544354003c, branch t0229-research-absent-cells before
salvage)

**Alibaba stage 3 → 2025-01-24.** Qwen Chat v0.2 launch on
chat.qwen.ai. Primary source: `@Alibaba_Qwen` X status
`1882818582758961351` (snowflake decode: 2025-01-24T15:51 UTC).
Cross-confirmed via the 2025-01-27 `qwen2.5-1m` blog post which
references Qwen Chat as supporting "perform searches".

The t0229 research also re-verified DeepSeek stage 5 absence via a
sweep of `api-docs.deepseek.com/news/` (15 entries from 2024-07-25
through 2026-04-24 V4 Preview). That finding is already reflected in
current main with a stronger note citing V3.1/V3.1-Terminus/V3.2
model-component components; t0229's news-index citation is
supplementary evidence, not a new decision.

